# Clean Code Skill

Based on Robert C. Martin (Clean Code)

## Principles

- Functions must be small and do one thing
- Use meaningful and intention-revealing names
- Prefer clarity over comments
- Avoid deep nesting (use early returns)
- Eliminate duplication (DRY)

## Detailed Guidance

- One level of abstraction per function
- Avoid boolean flags → split functions instead
- Keep code readable like prose
- Prefer composition over conditionals

## Error Handling

- Fail fast
- Never swallow errors
- Use explicit handling

## Cursor Behavior

- Rewrite unclear code
- Refuse messy but working code
- Optimize for readability and maintainability

## Sources

- Clean Code – Robert C. Martin
